# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit. Deny-by-default for key material.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by SHAPE, not by exact name: a key that leaks does so under a name nobody
# listed — did_seed.txt, identity.pem.bak, seed_backup.txt. Every pattern below
# is a substring or an extension family, so a variant is ignored by default and
# has to be un-ignored on purpose.
#
# The cost is documentation: `*seed*`, `*token*` and `*private*` also swallow a
# file like research/seed-strategy.md or a tokenomics note. That is deliberate —
# the rule holds and the *filename* moves. Run `git status --ignored` before a
# commit that adds documents, and rename anything caught.
secrets/
**/secrets/
secrets*
*.key
*key*.hex
*.pem
*.pem.*
*.seed
*seed*
*.priv
*private*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials*
*credential*
*token*
*.p12
*.pfx
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# Local agent state that may embed identifiers/nonces
**/state/
*.local.json
nonce.json

# Logs (may contain full signed URLs = replayable capability URLs)
**/logs/*
!**/logs/.gitkeep

# Third-party checkouts (read-only reference, not ours to vendor)
vendor/

# Noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.uvcache/
.DS_Store

# d-bitflop runtime state (HANDOFF.md §5.1): observations, exports, proof logs
data/
**/data/
export-*.jsonl
*.export.jsonl
proof.log
approval*.json
approval*.json.*
run-latest.json
market-latest.json

# Harness scratch: isolated subagent worktrees (auto-cleaned), never repository content
.claude/worktrees/
